WEBVTT

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.410
I guess 777's out.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.620
Look there.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.250
That's his choker.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.170
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.420
Miyashita Park Underpass

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.970
Rhyme and Beat

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:58.890
Where am I?

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.190
An underpass. Is this Miyashita Park?

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.310
Where'd Beat wander off to?

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.950
Was there an accident?

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.410
Hey, Beat.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.790
Whoa!

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.000
Yo, you're awake?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.420
Yeah. Looks like this is
our starting point today.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.090
We've gotta find Konishi.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.670
Oh, yeah.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.840
Hey, what's up? You've been acting weird.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.510
Huh? Well...

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.060
This is as good a time as any.
I'll tell you everything.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.060
Beat!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.320
Come on, Beat! Wait up!

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.860
He'll understand if you just talk to him.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.610
I've got nothing to say to
that hard-headed old man.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.330
But you know what they say:
"Haste makes waste."

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.000
Can it! Leave me alone.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.330
Beat.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.220
Rhyme!

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:26.140
Me and Rhyme died here.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.650
We got hit by an out-of-control car.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.860
Next thing I knew, we were
in the Underground.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.240
So, that's your deal.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.240
You see, Rhyme had a dream.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.500
If I'd listened to her,
she'd never have died.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.420
But because she had me for a brother...

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.590
Brother?!

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.050
Yeah.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:57.130
Rhyme's my kid sister.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.550
She is?!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.140
Nice to meet you.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.230
Huh? We've never met, have we?

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.020
She'd forgotten all about me.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.570
That was her entry fee?

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.820
She said she remembered having a brother,

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.990
but not his face, or name, or anything.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.790
That really got me down.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.080
Still, I made a Partner Pact with her,

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.710
so I was all psyched up to
keep her safe for sure this time.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.090
But I was the one who
ended up getting saved.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.430
It was my fault she died. Again.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:47.180
But you put your life on
the line to save her, right?

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:53.560
It didn't look like Rhyme held
anything against you to me.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.570
Your entry fee is something
you really care about.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:03.280
Doesn't that prove how
much she cared about you?

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.200
I ain't so sure.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.500
She was too nice for her own good.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:15.590
Maybe she was just lookin' out for me,
even though I'm a dumbass.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.630
Yeah, maybe.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:22.090
You're dumb all right.
Nothing's gonna fix that.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:26.180
Yo, was that necessary?

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.270
There aren't many idiots

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.020
who'd betray the Reapers to make
a pact with someone in my shoes.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:39.860
Before now, I never cared
about how others saw me.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.150
But...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:47.620
...when someone risks their life to
help me, I feel like I've gotta trust them.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.120
I was glad that you came to save me.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.500
I believe...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.590
...in your idiocy.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.260
Do you have to put it like that?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.930
It's a compliment.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:07.930
So, act like an idiot
and only look forward.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.560
Yeah.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.150
I guess you're right.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.060
I'll do it!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.690
No matter what, I'll save Rhyme and get
her back to normal and back to life!

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.910
Neku!

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.700
I owe you, man!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.200
No problem.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.210
Let's get Rhyme back.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.960
And Shiki too!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.420
Right?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.960
Yeah.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.800
Let's take out the Reapers
and go find Ironface!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.430
Hey, wait.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:48.680
What gives, man?

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:51.600
We've got to do our best to blend in.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.980
We're the only Players.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:07:01.320
If we fight flashy and the Reapers
call for backup, we'll be in trouble.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.740
We'll use keypins.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.740
Try the one 777 gave us yesterday.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.410
This thing?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.290
Let's go.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.040
Isn't it usually more crowded?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.010
Maybe there's an event goin' on somewhere?

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:26.470
This'll make it harder to blend in.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:27.840
--Hide!
--Hey!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.890
Have you seen those Players?

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:33.720
I thought I did a second ago,
but then I lost them.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.730
I'll check over on Route 3.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:36.890
Got it.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.860
We're gettin' nowhere.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.440
Yo, let's take a chance.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.860
We'll grab one of these
Reapers and scan 'em!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.910
We can't scan Reapers.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.700
We can only scan humans in the Real...

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.460
Easy for you to say,

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.130
but we won't get anywhere without clues.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.510
What was that just now?

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:09.890
What's up? You got a stomachache?

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.980
It really doesn't work. I can't scan them.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.810
What? No way.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:22.980
These guys are alive.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.940
You sure they weren't just spacing out?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.820
It wasn't like that.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.570
It's hard to explain,

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.910
but they were... empty.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.790
Any luck?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.580
I got nothing.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.670
I thought so.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.090
What gives?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.340
I don't know.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.390
Yo, Neku!

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.350
What?

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.060
Check that out!

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.730
A Red Skull pin.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.480
And it ain't just that one. Look around.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.940
They're all wearin' Red Skull pins.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.530
What's going on?

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:13.700
Hey, CAT designed the
Red Skull pins, right?

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.700
Yeah.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.330
Then...

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:20.040
...did CAT make the Player pins too?

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.750
They look the same to me.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:27.550
Remember what Shiki and Rhyme said?
Players can't scan each other.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.720
So, if we can't scan anybody
with a Red Skull pin,

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.720
the same guy must've made 'em.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:42.810
Player pins are designed and
controlled by the Composer.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:47.020
Who the hell <i>is </i>CAT anyway?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.360
CAT is Mr. Hanekoma.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.200
Mr. Hanekoma couldn't be the Composer.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.370
Joshua wouldn't have been looking
for the Composer if he were.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.120
Right now...

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.120
...finding Konishi comes first.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.500
You got it!

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.010
Hey, Uzuki,

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:15.430
maybe you shouldn't have taken
that special job for Ms. Konishi.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:16.640
Isn't it a drag?

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:20.390
You be quiet! I want a promotion!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:25.480
What's so great about being a big shot?
They lounge around and do nothing.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.820
Where's the fun in that?

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:31.990
Unlike you, I'm right on the edge!

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:35.570
Hmm. I'm not so sure about that.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.160
Anyway!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.740
I've got to make sure I don't
let Ms. Konishi down!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.790
We've got Reaper work to do!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.170
Tipsy Tose Hall

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:56.140
Look. Noise just keeps
pouring out of that place.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.640
Gimme a Red Skull pin!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.600
I'm terribly sorry. We're done
giving them out for today.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.110
--Do you know how long we've waited?!
--Cut the crap! I know you've got some!

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:07.770
What's that about?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.320
It's the source of the Noise.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.320
That's right!

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:14.110
They're feeding on negative
emotions and keep multiplying.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:17.870
Yo! Look at that!

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.530
What?

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.700
Ain't that Shiki?! What's she
doing in the Realground?!

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.500
No, that's Shiki's friend.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.710
Shiki's appearance got
taken as her entry fee.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.720
I don't really get it,
but we've gotta help her.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.060
There's no end to--

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.320
Neku, now!

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.150
Let 'em have it!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.330
All right! I knew you could do it!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.830
Guess I'll leave.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.630
I'll come back tomorrow.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.420
Oh well. Let's try other places.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.630
Good idea.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:18.550
I guess we'll have to
give up on Red Skull pins.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:22.180
They're so popular it's
weird to <i>not </i>have one.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:23.680
Let's look again.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.520
Stop goofing off!

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.690
You must be confident if you're
taking time out to fight Noise.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:39.150
Don't you care about this thing
I'm holding onto for Ms. Konishi?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.280
Rhyme!

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:44.330
We're going to need you to
play along with our mission.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:50.620
If we clear your mission,
you'll give us back Rhyme?

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.090
For now, anyway.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:56.130
What've we gotta do? Spit it out!

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.180
Your mission is...

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.560
Bring it on, assholes!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.650
Whoa!

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.730
Wh-What the hell?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.360
Oh, you're awake!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.450
Their mission came in!

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:23.820
Our mission for you is to fight us.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:27.780
Our mission for you is to fight us

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:27.700
We're gonna beat down Pinky
and Lollipop and get Rhyme back!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.870
Pretty straightforward mission.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.170
Get ready, Neku,

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:36.300
'cause Lollipop--Kariya--is real bad news.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.470
I hear he's as tough as an officer.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.970
Not every day I get a warning from you.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.720
What was that?!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.180
Anyway, go all out on this one!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.060
Got it.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.930
OK! Let's go!

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.060
H-Hey!

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.230
Go where?

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.020
After them!

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:59.110
Every Reaper's got one place
they hang out and watch Players!

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.650
Where's their turf?

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.570
Scramble Crossing

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.990
Scramble Crossing!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.160
Where now?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.580
Where are they?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.090
So, you finally showed up.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.550
Good grief. It's been ages
since I made an effort.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:24.130
In that case, let's liven things up.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.980
The people and cars are...

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:39.320
Go!

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.780
Bring it!

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.490
Get lost!

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.040
If you just focus on her,

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.540
you're gonna lose.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.590
I ain't done yet!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.460
All right, here I come!

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.060
That was almost a close one.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.310
I can see you've... grown!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:28.990
Uzuki.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.000
Bye-bye now.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.260
Ugh! I was just getting to the fun part!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.430
Stay still, damn it! What a pain!

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:02.820
If you let your guard down,
it'll cost you.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.360
Damn it.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.280
You OK, Neku?!

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.240
Yeah.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:12.530
It'll take more than this to beat me.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.740
Yeah!

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:21.920
What's that?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.880
They're not half bad.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.170
Let's make this count.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.840
Yeah, let's go!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.770
No one told me about this!

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:40.270
You're the ones who need...

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.440
...to take us seriously!

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:55.330
Give back Rhyme.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.540
Bravo. You win.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:02.710
We surrender.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:05.750
As promised, we'll return her.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.130
What?!

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.380
Hey!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.590
Rhyme!

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.430
Rhyme!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.440
Hey! What the hell?!

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:20.810
I thought so.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.940
Cut the crap! You pulled a fast one on me!

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.610
We didn't lie!

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:30.030
Ms. Konishi personally
left that in our care!

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.490
I'd say Ms. Konishi tricked us.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.790
She just used us to buy time.
We're disposable.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.750
No way!

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.290
No use complaining. We <i>are </i>underlings.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.920
Like hell there's not!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.420
They always treat us like this!

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.550
I'm sick of being on the bottom!

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:52.430
I know they were going to make you
an officer, and you turned them down!

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:55.300
Were you trying to spare my feelings?!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:58.100
Being an officer sucks.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:03.270
I like being on the ground.
I like Shibuya.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:08.110
A jumble of ideas collide.
People change, and so does the city.

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:12.400
I'm a stargazer who keeps his
eyes on those changes, basically.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.780
Plus, if I were an officer,

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.830
I couldn't grab a bite with you
when I feel like it, Uzuki.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.120
That time means a lot to me.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.540
Wh-What?

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.210
You done chatting?

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.960
Now, where the hell is Rhyme?!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.670
Probably still with Ms. Konishi.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.010
Sorry we put you through all that, man.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.760
This'll make up for it.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.640
A keypin.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:45.150
That'll get you into the
same places as an officer's.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.270
Don't you want your friend back?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.650
Yo, Mr. Kariya.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:54.610
Why'd you get so formal?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.910
Watch out for Ironface!

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:00.790
She erased the last Reaper
who gave us a keypin.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:03.540
She might come after you guys too.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:05.830
Thanks for the heads up.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.170
We'll take care of ourselves.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.340
Right, Uzuki?

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.510
Of course. We don't need <i>your </i>help.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:17.140
Well, see you.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:22.770
Tomorrow's the day we get Ironface.

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:23.850
You said it.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.730
Ah! You're not psyched-up enough!

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:29.570
Shout from way down in your gut!

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.190
Come on!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.280
We're...

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.070
...gonna...

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.700
...win!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:37.530
We're gonna win.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.330
Hey, should you have
given them that keypin?

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:47.710
If Ms. Konishi finds out,
we won't get off with a pay cut.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:53.590
Haven't you noticed, Uzuki?

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.670
Noticed what?

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.760
The changes in Shibuya.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.140
It's turning homogeneous.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:03.140
Now that you mention it,

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:07.850
the thoughts are usually obnoxiously loud,
but I don't hear many now.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:12.110
Yeah. The jumbled ideas
of Shibuya are slowly

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.990
but surely focusing into a single point.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.950
We can only pray that
point won't be a period.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.330
What's wrong?

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:25.040
No clue.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:27.080
I just...

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.420
Uzuki?!

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.250
Hey, what's wrong?!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.100
Konishi.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:48.640
I see the O-Pins' side effects
have begun to show.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:52.360
These won't be sparing us
deaths on the job.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.150
Hey, you knew this was going to happen?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.280
I don't know what
Mr. Kitaniji is thinking.

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:03.160
Why is the Composer
leaving those on the loose?

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.450
I need data.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:09.330
My plan demands hard facts.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.170
Shit.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.840
I won't...

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:42.610
The fundamentals of the
design are no good.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.620
Looks like this is all I can do.

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:51.330
Now...

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:56.460
...what comes next,

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.260
God only knows.

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:46.980
The Countless Wrongs of Our Day

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.660
"The Countless Wrongs of Our Day."
